From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: mt6789-zinwa-q25: reserve the MD1 image region

LK reserved the modem image region at 0xdc000000; with the DRAM ranks
from the boot tags it became System RAM, and q25-md1-owner could not
claim it (-EADDRINUSE). Carve it out as no-map so that the EFI memory
map keeps it from Linux.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts b/arch/arm/dts/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
--- a/arch/arm/dts/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/mt6789-zinwa-q25.dts
@@ -44,6 +44,12 @@
 		#size-cells = <0x02>;
 		ranges;
 
+		/* MD1 image, as LK reserved it; Marathon loads the modem here. */
+		md1-image@dc000000 {
+			reg = <0x00 0xdc000000 0x00 0x8000000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		mblock-33-shared-dma-pool_wifi-reserve-memory_dma {
 			reg = <0x00 0xbf000000 0x00 0x600000>;
 			no-map;
